---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Cloud & Supabase Auth Guide" currentPath="/docs/guides/cloud-supabase-auth">
  <div class="space-y-8 font-mono text-xs">
    <div>
      <div class="text-[11px] text-zinc-400 font-semibold mb-1">CLOUD EDITION</div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-sans">RouteNex Cloud & Supabase Authentication</h1>
      <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm font-sans mt-1">Multi-tenant authentication, workspace RBAC, and Supabase RLS migrations.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-[#111113] border border-[#222226] space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-white font-sans">Dual-Edition Model</h2>
      <div class="space-y-2 text-zinc-400">
        <div>• <strong class="text-white">RouteNex Open Source:</strong> 100% self-hosted, offline, and zero-cloud authentication required. Launches locally with direct terminal setup tokens.</div>
        <div>• <strong class="text-white">RouteNex Cloud:</strong> Multi-tenant managed platform powered by Supabase Auth with GitHub/Google OAuth, Magic Links, team RBAC, and centralized billing.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-[#111113] border border-[#222226] space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-white font-sans">Database Migration & Row-Level Security</h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
        Apply <code class="text-zinc-200">cloud/supabase-migration.sql</code> to your PostgreSQL instance to create the required tables (<code class="text-white">cloud_users</code>, <code class="text-white">organizations</code>, <code class="text-white">workspaces</code>, <code class="text-white">cloud_api_keys</code>, <code class="text-white">spend_accounting</code>) with strict RLS policies.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
